# Development Principles

- Prefer simple solutions that solve the requested problem.
- Do not introduce unnecessary abstractions.
- Do not create generic repositories, unit-of-work wrappers, or service layers just for architecture.
- Organize backend functionality by use case / vertical slice.
- Keep unrelated features isolated.
- Do not implement future features, placeholders for unexpected work, or speculative endpoints unless explicitly asked.
- Add packages, infrastructure, or cross-cutting concerns only when required by the current task.
